<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James Scullin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1876–1953</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James Scullin was the Labor prime minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> from 1929 to 1932, taking office just before the Wall Street Crash. His government struggled with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-depression">Great Depression</a>, falling export prices and heavy debts, and the Labor Party split over the response. He appointed Isaac Isaacs as the first Australian-born governor-general and lost office at the election of December 1931.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-scullin.jpg" alt="James Scullin" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: National Library of Australia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_James_H._Scullin_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
